<title>BELGIUM: Belgium sells 2.5 bln Bfr state notes on first day.</title>
<headline>Belgium sells 2.5 bln Bfr state notes on first day.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian finance ministry said on Thursday an issue of state notes raised 2.507 billion Belgian francs after one day of subscriptions.</p>
<p>The ministry said it sold 1.762 billion francs of five-year notes, extendable to seven years, which carry a fixed coupon of 4.90 percent. Notes with revisable coupons and put options after three, five and seven years have raised 745 million francs.</p>
<p>Subscriptions close on December 17.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
